{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nS1 [rebar:1934-63dd-4be9-4c48] lets a ticket explicitly assert\n`file_impact_scope: none`. S2 [rebar:749c-7546-6fe3-4d27] gives that assertion\nreal leverage: an authenticated `file-scope: none` attestation is not invalidated\nby unrelated HEAD movement. The assertion therefore needs a correctness check;\notherwise a false declaration could silence drift protection.\n\nThe check belongs in plan review, where the ticket plan, acceptance criteria,\ndeclared scope, and `no_file_impact_reason` are already available. It must be\nnarrow: it runs only when the persisted scope is exactly `none`; tickets with\n`paths` or `undeclared` scope must not incur an LLM call or finding.\n\n## Approach\n\nAdd one advisory LLM criterion, `no-file-impact`, whose sole judgment is whether\na ticket that declares no repository-file impact actually describes work that\nrequires changing a repository file.\n\n### Deterministic applicability\n\nFollow the existing `require_parent_id` routing-axis pattern:\n\n- Add `applies_at.require_file_impact_scope: [\"none\"]` to the packaged routing\n  entry for `no-file-impact`.\n- Extend the shared routing validator in\n  `src/rebar/llm/criteria/overlay.py` to accept and type-check the new\n  string-list key.\n- Extend `registry.applies(...)` with a `file_impact_scope` keyword and require\n  membership when a criterion declares this routing key.\n- Pass `ctx.state.get(\"file_impact_scope\")` at the single orchestrator call site.\n\nExisting criteria omit the key and retain their current behavior.\n\n### Criterion judgment and prompt discovery\n\nCreate `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_no_file_impact.md` with\n`category: plan-review-criterion`, `exec: 1-TURN`, facet `scope-intent`,\nadvisory posture, and a 0.95 block threshold. Plan-review criterion prompts are\nauto-discovered from their front matter by the packaged prompt scan; do not edit\nthe generated `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/index.json`, which only indexes\n`category: review` prompts.\n\nThe rubric distinguishes:\n\n- `assertion_plausible: yes` — all deliverables occur outside the repository;\n  return PASS with no finding.\n- `assertion_plausible: no` — the plan or acceptance criteria require changing\n  any repository file, including documentation; return an advisory finding that\n  cites the conflicting deliverable and coaches declaring the actual paths.\n- `assertion_plausible: insufficient` — evidence is too weak to decide; return\n  non-blocking coaching to strengthen `no_file_impact_reason`.\n\nReading or analysing repository code without editing it remains compatible with\n`none`. A docs-only change is not compatible because documentation is still a\nrepository file.\n\n### Declared-reason data flow\n\nRead `ctx.state.get(\"no_file_impact_reason\", \"\")` in the orchestrator and carry\nit into Pass 1. Extend the existing per-criterion `extra_context` construction\nin `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py` so a chunk containing\n`no-file-impact` receives a structured `declared_reason` field alongside the\nplan text. The criterion prompt renders that field. Do not add a dedicated\n`PlanContext` attribute.\n\n### Registration and generated documentation\n\n- Add `no-file-impact` to `CANONICAL_LLM`.\n- Add its packaged routing entry, including\n  `require_file_impact_scope: [\"none\"]`.\n- Regenerate `docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md` with the repository generator;\n  do not hand-edit the generated section.\n\n## Test Design\n\nTests must assert observable behavior and public contracts, never grep source\ntext or depend on private implementation shape.\n\n- Applicability contract: invoke the real criterion-selection path with persisted\n  ticket states `none`, `paths`, and `undeclared`; assert `no-file-impact` is\n  selected only for `none`.\n- Prompt-input contract: render the real Pass-1 request for a `none` ticket and\n  assert the persisted declared reason is present in the structured criterion\n  context. This verifies data flow at the LLM boundary, not source text.\n- Offline rubric behavior: exercise the criterion through the existing offline\n  judge fixture with (1) an external operator action that passes, (2) a plan\n  requiring a new CLI flag that produces an advisory finding, and (3) a\n  docs-only plan that produces an advisory finding directing the author to\n  declare documentation paths.\n- Public explain contract: invoke `rebar explain no-file-impact` and assert a\n  successful exit plus the criterion's semantic identity/usage in output.\n- Advisory gate contract: feed a criterion-only FAIL through the real verdict\n  aggregation path and assert the ticket remains claimable.\n- Generated-artifact contract: run the criteria-guide generator twice and assert\n  the tracked guide is byte-identical after each run.\n\nThe held-out oracle will include boundary scope values and advisory aggregation,\nand will use a defect-seeded mutation of the routing predicate to prove the\nbehavioral tests fail. Behavior-preserving renames or extraction must not break\nthe tests.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_no_file_impact.md` — criterion rubric.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/criteria_routing.json` — packaged routing entry.\n- `src/rebar/llm/criteria/overlay.py` — shared routing-key validation.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/registry.py` — canonical membership and\n  applicability predicate.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/orchestrator.py` — persisted scope/reason input.\n- `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py` — structured declared-reason context.\n- `docs/plan-review-criteria-guide.md` — generated criterion documentation.\n- Focused tests in the existing plan-review, routing, prompt, CLI, and gate test\n  modules selected after the required coverage inventory.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A ticket whose persisted `file_impact_scope` is `none` routes\n  `no-file-impact` into the Pass-1 finder set.\n- [ ] Tickets whose persisted scope is `paths` or `undeclared` do not route the\n  criterion or incur its LLM work.\n- [ ] The criterion passes work whose deliverables are all outside the repository.\n- [ ] The criterion emits an advisory finding when source, configuration, tests,\n  or documentation must change in the repository.\n- [ ] An insufficient declaration produces non-blocking coaching to strengthen\n  `no_file_impact_reason`.\n- [ ] The exact persisted reason reaches the rendered criterion request through\n  the production Pass-1 path.\n- [ ] `no-file-impact` is canonical, its packaged routing validates, and\n  `rebar explain no-file-impact` succeeds with the criterion documentation.\n- [ ] The regenerated criteria guide is byte-identical to a fresh second\n  regeneration.\n- [ ] A failure from this advisory criterion alone does not block claim.\n- [ ] New tests are behavior/contract-focused and remain green under\n  behavior-preserving refactors; no source-grep/change-detector tests are added.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the full test suite pass."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785227795894017001,"uuid":"568306d3-a9d9-4e99-8478-e98efd5136bf"}